module

public import QED.DimReg.ThreeLoopPoly

/-!
# Annihilators of `G^(-d/2)` for the twelve IBP templates of the set (d) family

For each IBP template `(i, j)` of `QED.ThreeLoopD.SetDCert.lbl` (`i < 3` loop momenta
differentiated, `j < 4` momenta in the numerator) an untrusted generator (`ann3.py`) solved,
over `ℚ`, for a vector field `p = (p_b)_b` of degree `≤ 2` and a multiplier `q` of degree
`≤ 1` with

  `Σ_b p_b ∂_b G = q G`  (no remainder),

such that the relation of `QED.DimReg.lpIntegral_annihilator` for `J(ν, d) = ∫ x^(ν-1) G^(-d/2)`,
multiplied by the Lee–Pomeransky normalization `Γ(d/2) / (Γ(2d - |ν|) ∏_a Γ(ν_a))` of each
term, is exactly the template relation `QED.Algebra.IBPCert.Family.template i j` (coefficient
by coefficient, as rational functions of `(ν, d)`). All solutions have integer coefficients;
the free parameters were set to `0`. For `j < 2` (numerator `k₁`, `k₂`) the vector field is
linear and, except for `(0, 0)` and `(1, 1)`, `q = 0`.

Here the syzygies are checked by the kernel (`annCheck_all`, via
`QED.DimReg.ZPoly.annCheck`), and stated in the form required by
`QED.DimReg.lpIntegral_annihilator` (`hsyz`, `he`). The template matching is the
normalization step of the IBP layer, carried out when the continued integrals are defined.

## Main results

* `QED.DimReg.ThreeLoop.pT`, `QED.DimReg.ThreeLoop.qT`: the data.
* `QED.DimReg.ThreeLoop.annCheck_all`: the twelve syzygies.
* `QED.DimReg.ThreeLoop.hsyz`, `QED.DimReg.ThreeLoop.he`.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace QED.DimReg.ThreeLoop

open QED.DimReg.Sector QED.DimReg.ZPoly

